# Sample BUFR File

This is a placeholder for a sample BUFR file.

## Description

A sample BUFR file containing observational meteorological data for testing and demonstration purposes.

## Typical Contents

- Surface observations: Temperature, humidity, pressure, wind
- Upper air soundings: Vertical profiles of temperature, humidity, wind
- Satellite observations: Radiances, brightness temperatures
- Marine observations: Sea surface temperature, wave data

## File Size

Typical size: 100 KB - 10 MB depending on number of observations

## How to Obtain

Sample BUFR files can be obtained from:
- ECMWF Observation Data: https://www.ecmwf.int/en/observations/data-licensing
- NOAA IGRA: https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/products/bufr/igra/
- WMO BUFR Tables: https://www.wmo.int/pages/prog/www/WMOCodes.html

## Example Usage

```python
import eccodes

with open('sample_bufr.bufr', 'rb') as f:
    msg_id = eccodes.codes_bufr_new_from_file(f)
    
    # Unpack message
    eccodes.codes_set(msg_id, 'unpack', 1)
    
    # Get observation data
    lat = eccodes.codes_get(msg_id, 'latitude')
    lon = eccodes.codes_get(msg_id, 'longitude')
    temp = eccodes.codes_get(msg_id, 'airTemperature')
    
    print(f"Location: ({lat}, {lon})")
    print(f"Temperature: {temp} K")
    
    eccodes.codes_release(msg_id)
```

## Notes

- This is a text placeholder file
- Actual BUFR files are binary and cannot be represented as text
- Replace this file with an actual BUFR file for testing